{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.ConstantKernelGrowthBound","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.ConstantKernelGrowthBound","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.BigOperators.Group.Finset","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ConstantKernelGrowthBound.not_superExponential_of_isConstKernelRec","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ConstantKernelGrowthBound.not_superExponential_of_isConstKernelRec","kind":"theorem","line":186,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ConstantKernelGrowthBound.lean#L186-L192","doc":"Contrapositive in the direction a reader holding the fixed-depth proposition\nwill want it: if the periods really do satisfy a constant-kernel recurrence,\nthey are **not** super-exponential — so the identification with `I n / n` fails,\nor the abelianisation does. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ConstantKernelGrowthBound.not_isConstKernelRec_of_superExponential","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ConstantKernelGrowthBound.not_isConstKernelRec_of_superExponential","kind":"theorem","line":173,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ConstantKernelGrowthBound.lean#L173-L184","doc":"**The contradiction.** No super-exponentially growing sequence satisfies a\ndepth-`d` recurrence with a constant kernel, for any depth and any kernel.\n\nApplied to the corpus: `prop:prolonged-periods-fixed-depth` (constant kernel,\n`d ≤ 8`) and `classical_period_ratio_unbounded` (super-exponential) cannot both\nhold of `a_D^(n)`. Which one gives is not decided here — see the file header. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ConstantKernelGrowthBound.exists_exponential_bound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ConstantKernelGrowthBound.exists_exponential_bound","kind":"theorem","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ConstantKernelGrowthBound.lean#L110-L171","doc":"**The bound.** Every solution of a depth-`d` constant-kernel recurrence is\ndominated by a geometric sequence whose base is the kernel's `ℓ¹` norm (or `1`,\nwhichever is larger) and whose constant depends only on the `d` initial values.\n\nThis is the elementary form of \"constant-coefficient recurrences have solutions\n`Σ p_i n * λ_i ^ n`\" — stated as a bound so that it can be contradicted by a\ngrowth hypothesis without needing the characteristic-root decomposition. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ConstantKernelGrowthBound.kernelBound_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ConstantKernelGrowthBound.kernelBound_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ConstantKernelGrowthBound.lean#L107-L108","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ConstantKernelGrowthBound.sum_abs_le_kernelBound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ConstantKernelGrowthBound.sum_abs_le_kernelBound","kind":"theorem","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ConstantKernelGrowthBound.lean#L104-L105","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ConstantKernelGrowthBound.one_le_kernelBound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ConstantKernelGrowthBound.one_le_kernelBound","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ConstantKernelGrowthBound.lean#L102-L102","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ConstantKernelGrowthBound.kernelBound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ConstantKernelGrowthBound.kernelBound","kind":"def","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ConstantKernelGrowthBound.lean#L98-L100","doc":"The kernel's `ℓ¹` norm, and the base of the geometric bound. Taking the max\nwith `1` is what makes the bound monotone in the exponent. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ConstantKernelGrowthBound.SuperExponential","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ConstantKernelGrowthBound.SuperExponential","kind":"def","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ConstantKernelGrowthBound.lean#L93-L96","doc":"`a` grows **super-exponentially**: it eventually exceeds every geometric\nsequence. This is the shape of `classical_period_ratio_unbounded`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ConstantKernelGrowthBound.IsConstKernelRec","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ConstantKernelGrowthBound.IsConstKernelRec","kind":"def","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ConstantKernelGrowthBound.lean#L87-L91","doc":"`a` satisfies a depth-`d` linear recurrence with the **constant** (that is,\n`n`-independent) kernel `c`. This is the hypothesis\n`prop:prolonged-periods-fixed-depth` asserts of the prolongation periods. ","signatureChunk":0}]}